message: "If you use FEM LAB in teaching or research, please cite it using this metadata."
title: "FEM LAB: interactive one-dimensional Galerkin finite elements"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "yzd-info"
repository-code: "https://github.com/yzd-info/fem-lab"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Interactive teaching tool for one-dimensional linear differential equations solved with the Galerkin finite element
  method (Lagrange P1-P4), with step-by-step visualization, a symbolic solution sheet and independent verification.
references:
  - type: book
    title: "The Finite Element Method: Basic Concepts and Applications with MATLAB, MAPLE, and COMSOL"
    authors:
